    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n55642" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατα-χύδην</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῠ]</span>, Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>pouring down, profusely</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πίνειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anacr.
					90
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατά-χῠμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>, τό,
				<i>bath-water</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ammon.
				<u>Diff.</u>
				p.78
			</span></i> V.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ.</span>, =
			<i>perfusio</i> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ζωμοῦ</span>,
				=
			<i>tucca,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gloss.
			</span></i>: but in pl., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταχύσματα</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Them.
				<u>Or.</u>
				23.293c
			</span></i>.</div>
